; Template for a new level. Copy to map<N>.map, where N is the level number
; loadMap() is given; anything not named that way is never loaded. The format
; is described in README.md beside this file. Lines starting with ; are
; comments and may be deleted.
;
; The grid is 64 rows of 64 cells, no spaces, no comments between the rows.
; Cell characters (getCellEncoding in game_map.c):
;   0 floor          X wall           P dark wall      V void
;   D door           T locked door    A archway        W window
;   S shootable      B bars           R low wall       | pillar
;   ! sign           * light          : pipes          # dado
;   U switch (opens every locked door)
;   C E F G  enemies (see getEnemyCell in enemy.c)
;   H..O     pickups (see getPickupCell in pickup.c)
;   1..8     decorations (see getDecorCell in decor.c)
; This grid is solid wall with an 8 x 6 room at the top left for the spawn.

